# What in this repository is written, and what is produced.
#
# `results/yatra.html` is committed on purpose -- a reader should be able to
# open the answer console without running the pipeline first -- but nobody
# wrote it. It is output: `make ui` regenerates it in full from `src/yatra/ui.py`
# and the artefacts in `results/`, and an edit made to it by hand would be gone
# on the next run. Marking it generated tells GitHub two true things: leave it
# out of the language statistics, which are meant to describe the source, and
# fold it in diffs, where two megabytes of regenerated markup is noise around
# the change that actually caused it.
#
# The stylesheet and the script the page carries are Python string constants in
# `ui.py` and are counted where they live, which is also where they are edited.
results/yatra.html linguist-generated=true
